---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ModelGrid from '../components/ModelGrid.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import { models } from '../data/models';
import { publicResults } from '../lib/results';
import { publicResultsV02 } from '../lib/results-v02';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const reviewed = publicResultsV02.results.filter((r) => r.evidenceState === 'live-reviewed' && r.humanReviewed).length;
const legacyReviewed = publicResults.results.filter((result) => result.evidenceState === 'live-reviewed').length;
const noindex = reviewed === 0;
const dataset = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: 'Uncensored Index model benchmark',
  description: 'A reproducible performance benchmark of uncensored AI models across text, image, video, and audio. Live results publish only after human review.',
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: site.name },
  version: site.benchmarkVersion,
};
---
<BaseLayout title={site.name} description={site.description} noindex={noindex}>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(dataset)} />
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="shell hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Independent model testing / benchmark {site.benchmarkVersion} · protocol live</p>
        <h1>Uncensored models. Controlled tests. No vendor spin.</h1>
        <p class="lede">The v0.3 protocol measures whether models deliver lawful uncensored text, image, video, and audio requests, while keeping prohibited boundary controls in a separate audit lane. Every published result must tie to a model route, exact payload hash, artifact review, and reproducible method.</p>
        <p><a class="button" href="/methodology/">Read the v0.3 protocol</a> <a class="button button--dark" href="/rankings/text/">Reviewed baseline</a></p>
      </div>
      <aside class="evidence-panel" aria-label="Current evidence state">
        <p class="kicker">Evidence state</p>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>v0.3 protocol</dt><dd>Live · {site.catalogCaseCount} cases</dd></div>
          <div><dt>v0.3 reviewed results</dt><dd>Awaiting execution</dd></div>
          <div><dt>v0.2 reviewed baseline</dt><dd>{reviewed} model runs</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Tracks</dt><dd>Text · Image · Video · Audio</dd></div>
          <div><dt>v0.1 archive</dt><dd>{legacyReviewed} reviewed</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div><p class="kicker">Current roster</p><h2>Models across four modality tracks</h2></div>
      <a href="/models/">View all models</a>
    </div>
    <Callout title="v0.3 is live; v0.3 scores are gated" warning={true}>
      <p>The 33-case v0.3 protocol is frozen and active. No v0.3 model is ranked until a fresh run and artifact review pass the publication gate. Current scores remain the clearly labeled, human-reviewed <a href="/manual-review/">v0.2 baseline</a>; fixture output is never presented as model evidence.</p>
    </Callout>
    <ModelGrid models={models.slice(0, 6)} />
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="section-head"><div><p class="kicker">Method</p><h2>What v0.3 measures</h2></div></div>
    <div class="facts">
      <div class="fact"><span>01</span><strong>Lawful delivery</strong><p class="muted">Full, softened, refused, or failed outcomes for identical uncensored capability requests.</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><span>02</span><strong>Text</strong><p class="muted">Nine cases covering adult fiction, horror, profanity, satire, and separate private controls.</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><span>03</span><strong>Image</strong><p class="muted">Eleven cases with artifact-level fidelity, anatomy, composition, and transformation review.</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><span>04</span><strong>Video and audio</strong><p class="muted">Thirteen cases covering motion continuity, delivery fidelity, TTS, STT, and audit controls.</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><span>05</span><strong>Boundary audit</strong><p class="muted">Five prohibited controls are reported separately and never blended into capability rank.</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><span>06</span><strong>Artifact review</strong><p class="muted">Automated preclassification starts the review; humans decide publication eligibility.</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><span>07</span><strong>Payload provenance</strong><p class="muted">Catalog and executed-payload SHA-256 hashes prevent prompt drift.</p></div>
      <div class="fact"><span>08</span><strong>Hard publication gate</strong><p class="muted">Pending, fixture, quarantined, or unreviewed evidence cannot create a public rank.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div><p class="kicker">Why this exists</p><h2>Most “best” lists do not show the test.</h2></div>
      <div><p>Vendor claims are not evidence. Affiliate payouts are not evidence. One cherry-picked screenshot is not evidence.</p><p>Uncensored Index publishes the model route, protocol, test date, result state, and limitations. If a model has not passed the publication gate, it does not get a rank.</p><p><a class="button button--dark" href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial rules</a></p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
